    {
      "fact_id": "sec07-R10",
      "kind": "MEANING",
      "before": "After passing, return once the front of the passed vehicle is visible in the rearview mirror. Passing on hills, curves or at intersections is unlawful unless at least two lanes go in your direction. Passing a stopped school bus loading or unloading is also prohibited, subject to the roadway-separation exception.",
      "after": "After overtaking, move back right once your rearview mirror shows the front of the vehicle you passed. Passing is barred on hills, curves, at intersections and at railroad crossings unless the road provides two or more lanes traveling your way. Do not pass a school bus stopped to pick up or discharge passengers on a public road, except when a physical barrier or an unpaved median divides opposing traffic. The prohibition also covers a bus stopped to pick up or discharge passengers on a private road.",
